<title>BELGIUM: EU clears GE/BankAmerica Spanish cable deal.</title>
<headline>EU clears GE/BankAmerica Spanish cable deal.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Friday it had approved a plan by U.S.-based General Electric Capital Services and BankAmerica International Investment to take joint control of Spanish cable TV operator Cableuropa SA.</p>
<p>Cableuropa announced in May that the two companies had taken a 32.5 percent stake in it through their joint venture Spain Telecommunications Ltd (Spainco).</p>
<p>&quot;Cableuropa will be confronted with active competition from other companies that are firmly established in the markets in question, notably Telefonica in telecommunications and Sogecable in the pay TV market,&quot; the Commission said in a statement.</p>
</text>
